#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:462
#: f1df021990f74aab9cd382e2010ab3b1
msgid "The `multi_uav_ros_sitl.launch file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Airsim/multi_uav_ros_sitl.launch>`__ demonstrates how to write a launch file controlling multiple vehicles with Mavros. It creates a different namespace for each drone and each drone has a separate SYSID and ports according to how the script sets the variables. Launching the file -"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:469
#: 523ec80b2e5346fca967e0f991207ffa
msgid "Separate MAVProxy instance can be launched for each drone by connecting to the TCP ports opened by the script for each drone. The UDP ports can't be used for this if Mavros is already running since Mavros will use the UDP ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:471
#: 11720641555946c8a847684bd1f3c43f
msgid "The ``multi_vehicle.sh`` script doesn't enable the Follow Mode, but if this is also needed and if all the vehicles are to be displayed on the same GCS, then multicast and the Follow parameters as done in the ``follow-copter.sh`` script can be added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:476
#: 7606d955ae1f4212ab9150168bba74e1
msgid "Custom Environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:478
#: 6974962a1b774a6ca940dc3b72935036
msgid "For using another environment on Windows, see `AirSim's custom env setup page <https://microsoft.github.io/AirSim/docs/unreal_custenv/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:481
#: 62acfe033507479a95adf9d9712c641a
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:483
#: 65a5a2a850104b5e86591497f3364454
msgid "As mentioned in the above-linked page, there is no Epic Games Launcher for Linux which means that if you need to use a custom environment, you will need Windows machine to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:485
#: 3c32dc35ac184df3b3243421cce133db
msgid "The steps are the same once you have the Windows machine, after you have downloaded the Unreal project, just copy the project over to your Linux machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:487
#: 237ce1ca263d42179c79548436f06314
msgid "Follow the steps till after Step 6 where you have edited the ``.uproject`` file. After editing the project file, skip Step 7,8 and directly start the Editor by going to UnrealEngine folder and start Unreal by running ``UnrealEngine/Engine/Binaries/Linux/UE4Editor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:489
#: fd69b68d94d94dc5ba3548649067ea95
msgid "When Unreal Engine prompts for opening or creating project, select Browse and select your custom environment. Afterwards, continue following the Steps from 9 onwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:493
#: 2a8cd44611e24d878e71d9ab77cb53da
msgid "When using a custom environment, it might be the case that there are multiple ``Player Start`` objects. In such a case, it randomly chooses one and the vehicle can start in the air and fall."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:495
#: 73cec52c6ecc4449ad9b0ecf1ae79e6f
msgid "You'll have to delete the extra ``Player Start`` objects and leave one which has to be moved to near the ground. See this excellent video by one of the AirSim developers - `Unreal AirSim Setup <https://youtu.be/1oY8Qu5maQQ>`__, specifically at 5:00 where it's demonstrated how to delete the objects and to move the position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:500
#: 8bc7f37576e6440783079c2b0c83ef9b
msgid "Using AirSim APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:502
#: 064ac64514d54c43880f6a8f3f88d126
msgid "`AirSim's APIs document <https://github.com/microsoft/AirSim/blob/master/docs/apis.md>`__ explains the different APIs available and their usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:504
#: 20ec6ebdbfc248129d4c0880c4070374
msgid "Currently, ArduPilot vehicles don't support controlling the movement through the AirSim APIs, however any method of controlling the movement which connects directly to ArduPilot rather than using AirSim’s API work, examples include DroneKit & ROS with Mavros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:506
#: 924599a1c20a4f16b7a831db1d766031
msgid "The `Image APIs <https://github.com/microsoft/AirSim/blob/master/docs/image_apis.md>`__ have been tested to work with Copter, for some ready-to-run sample codes, see the files in ``PythonClient/multirotor`` such as ``opencv_show.py``. Also, any APIs which are are used to fetch information about the environment, and interact with it, or even collect sensor information will work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:508
#: b70bd4254c2a4abbbcf0159e049b4b7e
msgid "A ROS wrapper has also been added. See `airsim_ros_pkgs <https://github.com/microsoft/AirSim/blob/master/docs/airsim_ros_pkgs.md>`__ for the ROS API, and `airsim_tutorial_pkgs <https://github.com/microsoft/AirSim/blob/master/docs/airsim_tutorial_pkgs.md>`__ for tutorials. Note that limitations of controlling vehicle movement exist here as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-airsim.rst:512
#: 3ed65fc719fc42498c7827e1d53e2b1c
msgid "Not all the APIs have been tested with Copter, if you find things that don't work or would like to have them supported, please let us know"
msgstr ""

